{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/398382-remembering-the-past-differently","id":398382,"title":"Remembering the past differently","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-08T21:17:41-08:00","id":398382,"title":"Remembering the past differently","content":"I was wondering if anyone has had this phenomenon happen to them. Do you remember things that happened but you can find no trace of it actually happening or people tell you it didn't happen. There are several things that I personally remember seeing and doing but no one else does or I can find no evidence of it happening. Here are some examples from my life.<br /> <br /> When I was about 6 or 7, I was standing on a small wall and looking down on one of two of my cousins laying on their backs talking. One of them had been mean to me so I picked up a small cement block and dropped it on his chest. I broke a rib I think as he had to go to the hospital. But, no one in my family remembers this happening. I remember it very well.<br /> <br /> I remember an episode of Star Trek: TOS where they had to fight shadow people who could appear anywhere. I remember Kirk talking to McCoy about them at the end of the show. McCoy was glad their troubles were over but Kirk asked how could they really be sure.<br /> <br /> I remember seeing an ad in the late 1980s for a movie coming out at Christmas time called Nutcracker. Of course it was a retelling of The Nutcracker but it stared Kiefer Sutherland. As far as I can tell there has never been such a movie, but I remember seeing the ad.<br /> <br /> There are many other things like this I remember. Has anyone else experienced anything like this? Just wondering.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T21:40:44-08:00","id":398417,"title":"","content":"That's a very common experience. The human memory is very fallible; there's some fascinating stuff to learn if you look up the findings of research on memory. I seem to recall hearing that the way the brain stores memories is iterative - it's like your brain tells itself a story all over again every time you remember something, and like with literal storytelling, the story can change in the telling, even when the audience is just yourself and it's all internal. I'm probably greatly misrepresenting the particulars, mind; I am not a neurologist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T06:04:16-08:00","id":398727,"title":"","content":"Sometimes I have vivid dreams of things that could plausibly have happened to me in real life, and on waking I have to take a bit of time to sort out things that actually did happen to me from things that I remember clearly but don't actually fit in the narrative of my life. On a few occasions I have dreamt out the course of an entire day, and then woke up thinking it was later in the week than it actually was.<br /> <br /> Memory and consciousness are confusing things. Journals, photos, and other bits of physical evidence can help to keep everything straight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 02-09-2015, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T07:52:04-08:00","id":398760,"title":"","content":"Maybe. If so &lt;tinfoil hat&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forever and always forward.<br /> Don't ask why that came to mind or that I felt the need to post it.<br /> I see the incorporeally challenged.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/787-sorwen","name":"Sorwen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T09:07:13-08:00","id":398804,"title":"","content":"And we wonder why nobody can ever remember what governments do when they purposely try to destroy memory... &lt;tinfoil&gt;<br /> <br /> Seriously, talk to people who have been involved with black programs, their memories get soooo damned sketchy as time goes by from spending so much time trying to make sure there's no trace (even of harmless junk).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T09:33:14-08:00","id":398841,"title":"","content":"It's called a &quot;glitch in The Matrix&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T10:52:02-08:00","id":399014,"title":"","content":"These memories I have aren't remembered dreams. I have a pretty good long term memory. I remember some things from before I was two. I remember dreams I had as a child. The thing I am talking about are memories of things that I have seen or done, but no one else remembers. I started keeping a list of things that I remember around the time I went to college. The list has grown some over the years as new things are add that no one else remembers and I can't find any proof of any more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T12:44:05-08:00","id":399192,"title":"","content":"So you have a list of things you remember no one else does? Try getting ahead of it with a journal of your day-to-day activities basis and then seeing if you start remembering things that aren't in your journal later (I'm serious).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T17:40:02-08:00","id":399619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David G</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/398382-remembering-the-past-differently#post398382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember seeing an ad in the late 1980s for a movie coming out at Christmas time called Nutcracker. Of course it was a retelling of The Nutcracker but it stared Kiefer Sutherland. As far as I can tell there has never been such a movie, but I remember seeing the ad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Check this out: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Nutcracker_Prince\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Nutcracker_Prince</a><br /> <br /> Came out in 1990 and was animated but it starred....Kiefer Sutherland. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> As for your memory issues, I'm with you. I miss remember things a lot, or lose memories. It's terrible.<br /> <br /> This reminds me, if you want to see an interesting Sci-Fi movie on memories, check out one called The Final Cut starring Robin Williams. I think you'll dig it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, maybe you're remembering things from alternate versions of yourself? You never know...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/398382-remembering-the-past-differently?p=398841#post398841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's called a &quot;glitch in The Matrix&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}